520 8  This publication is an experimental space. Rather than a 
       linear narrative, it follows an improvised internal logic.
       The Chinese scholar's garden was chosen as a spatial model
       for presenting the works of Olafur Eliasson in book format
       and for exploring the key philosophical concerns in his 
       artistic practice. The book contains extensive material 
       from a trip undertaken in February 2011 to the Master of 
       Nets Garden and the Lion Grove Garden, two scholar's 
       gardens in Suzhou, China. The journey explored the 
       traditional Chinese scholar's garden as a model for 
       physical movement, for duration, rhythm, and sequencing, 
       and also as inspiration for the present book. 
